{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/mule/classify.ts@L32","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/classify.ts","span":{"start":32,"end":37}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/classify.ts","span":{"start":32,"end":37},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:6c118a2c2b4198b907b9668d74ee83b5c7189dab9eb6fb2fc5c33199fc3ed968","meta":{"text":"True if `path` contains the directory `segment` as a path component — at the start of the path\nor after a leading slash — so a repo-root file (`src/test/munit/suite.xml`, no leading slash)\nand a nested-root file (`legacy/src/test/munit/order-test.xml`) both match `src/test/munit`.\nPlain `.includes('/src/test/munit/')` (leading slash) misses the repo-root case: a Mule project\nindexed at its own root (`crib index <project-dir>`) has projectRoot `''`, so every file path\nlacks the leading slash and MUnit files would misclassify as `config` instead of `munit`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/mule/classify.ts@L60","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/classify.ts","span":{"start":60,"end":63}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/classify.ts","span":{"start":60,"end":63},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:8c02fd6ee846fcf7f7c5a6cb41ea1db0b9703ad078141d2799717c45c849ce57","meta":{"text":"Normalize a config path to its project-relative logical key by stripping the JAR-packaging\nprefix (`classes/` or `META-INF/mule-src/`) and a leading Mule source-tree segment. A packaged\n`classes/api.xml` and its attached source `META-INF/mule-src/main/mule/api.xml` both reduce to\n`api.xml`. Paths carrying neither packaging prefix are returned unchanged (not deduped)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/mule/classify.ts@L74","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/classify.ts","span":{"start":74,"end":76}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/classify.ts","span":{"start":74,"end":76},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:fbe8ed370c9e5f63b7b42d67fa1fa622d198b42b702694cec43e5c1e1d936f94","meta":{"text":"True for the semantic XML roles that participate in attached-source dedup (config flows +\nMUnit tests). Descriptors, properties, DataWeave, and RAML are out of scope: the spec dedups\n\"packaged XML\" configs, and descriptors must stay classified to anchor a JAR's dialect."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/mule/classify.ts@L81","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/classify.ts","span":{"start":81,"end":82}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/mule/classify.ts","span":{"start":81,"end":82},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:b3da812082057e20388c0c02d5159a7aaf2606ea48b1df3561f0a09a5c0482e1","meta":{"text":"For one project's members, return the set of packaged `classes/` paths whose attached-source\noriginal is also present (attached source wins). Emits one bounded warning per skipped path."}}
